<title>USA: Andrew votes three-for-two stock split.</title>
<headline>Andrew votes three-for-two stock split.</headline>
<dateline>ORLAND PARK, Ill. 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andrew Corp said it Tuesday it will split its common stock three shares for two on March 11, to shareholders of record on February 25.</p>
<p>The company, which manufactures specialized antennas and transmission lines, had 60.6 million shares of common stock outstanding on December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;We're very happy to be able to split the stock for the fifth year in a row,&quot; said chairman Floyd English in remarks prepared for delivery to the company's annual shareholders meeting.</p>
<p>	  ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
</text>
